above\">ΙΕ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"καλανδῶν\">Κ\u003Cspan class=\"supraline\" title=\"line above\">ΑΛ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cbr id=\"al4-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"Ἀπριλίων\">ΑΠΡΙΛΙΩΝ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"ζή\n                    σας\">ΖΗ\u003Cbr id=\"al5-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">5\u003C/span>ΣΑΣ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"ἔτη\">ΕΤΗ\u003C/span>Ν\u003Cbr id=\"al6-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">6\u003C/span>Α𐆠Ω\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"facsimile-images\">\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"apparatus\">\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>\u003Cspan>Text: IG\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7077-0703\">Alex Antoniou\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>Ioulianos died 15 days before the Kalends of April, having lived for 50 years\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>The funerary inscription is Christian, as suggested by the particular attention devoted to recording the day of the deceased's death and by the final Christogram. For the name \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Ἰουλιανός\u003C/span> in Sicily, see IG XIV 126 (= \u003Ca href=\"https://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic000943\" target=\"_blank\">ISic000943\u003C/a>), from Syracuse.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Amico 1741 267 no. IX \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002186\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002186\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Kirchhoff 1877 9489 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001249\" targ